Retired generic USB implementation evidence (test-only)
=======================================================

No file here is imported by the default kernel or daemon. These files do not
establish standard USB hardware support or WS73 wire conformance.

sle_transport.rs and attach_metadata.rs preserve the previous registration
and metadata projection. The pending/open production source regression is
run_usb_registration.py; hardware acceptance is a separate VM gate.

legacy_usb_codec.rs preserves exact unused encoder/header-parser segments
from Linux 5a49caef5a6e8742d978fd66aa685b5b6472c68b. The old encoders silently
truncate and mask inputs; the header parser ignores reserved bits. These are
historical failure witnesses, not supported behavior. Do not restore this
codec to production. Actual USB transmission uses retained C context APIs.

run_usb_codec_isolation.py separately checks four bounds on the actual live
parse_event_packet body (errno/allocation dependencies are fixtures) and
three historical codec witnesses. It does not prove callback lifetime,
allocator failure handling, IRQ safety, module ownership, PM or radio I/O.

Unconsumed Rust low-level URB/sync wrappers and corresponding C OUT/sync
helpers have been deleted rather than maintained as a second transport API.
Actual C RX allocation/submit/kill/join and immutable registered ingress
callbacks remain in production. Full common Backend and bus/build migration
remains open in OpenSparklink/linux #4, #9, #10, #12, #14 and #19.
